proposed_comments.body:
**Severity: medium.** The toolkit intentionally copies the host-owned query arguments before starting asynchronous work. The exact upstream test fails at `AreSame`: the values may be correct while the new object cannot be reference-equal to `args`. If unchanged, this regression test fails before checking the returned snapshot. Preserve the copy boundary and compare its fields rather than changing production behavior to satisfy the assertion.

```suggestion
        Assert.IsNotNull(fallback.LastQuery);
        Assert.AreEqual(args.Query, fallback.LastQuery.Query);
        Assert.AreEqual(args.QueryId, fallback.LastQuery.QueryId);
        Assert.AreEqual(args.RequestedItemCount, fallback.LastQuery.RequestedItemCount);
        CollectionAssert.AreEqual(args.LanguageTags, fallback.LastQuery.LanguageTags);
```

**Verification:** The current toolkit project builds with analyzers enabled; its original fallback suite passes 12/13 and fails on the identity assertion. The minimal candidate passes 13/13, and the sample extension project builds. No host implementation or interactive UI execution is claimed.
